						</a>
		
											</div> <!-- .comment-meta -->
		
					<div class="comment-content">
						<p>By definition, the Statue of Liberty is a building. Tourists can go thru the entire stand and it&#8217;s floors, and inside the statue by stairs or elevator. The head has an indoor observatory. Until closed for safety, there are stairs and a passage way up to the torch, with a look out no longer in use. Same for the Eiffel Tower. Some of you have never been to these structures and have no idea what they are.</p>
						
												
			
