						</a>
		
											</div> <!-- .comment-meta -->
		
					<div class="comment-content">
						<p>I think that&#8217;s a pretty subjective definition. I believe that a building is a permanent structure with walls, at least one level and a roof. It&#8217;s primary purpose must be one that compliments typical building use (i.e. living, manufacturing, government, commerce etc.). As such, I would hesitate to include the Statue of Liberty in this group as it is primarily a statue.</p>
						
												
			
						<div class="reply">
														
						</div><!-- .reply -->
						
					</div>
				</article><!-- #comment-N -->
	
